% Demo: subscription_billing_after_python.prompt
%
% This is the AFTER state — the same billing-service prompt after
% `pdd checkup --prompt-repair best-effort` applied two passes:
%
%  Pass 1 (ADD_VOCABULARY ×5):
%    Defined "active", "valid", "graceful payment failure", "reasonable", "successful"
%    in a new <vocabulary> block.  VAGUE_TERM issues: 9 → 4.
%
%  Pass 2 (CLARIFY_VAGUE_TERM ×4):
%    Replaced vague observable-outcome phrases in R1/R2/R3/R4
%    with concrete HTTP verbs and status codes.  Issues: 4 → 0.
%
% Expected: 0 lint issues.
%
% Verify:
%   pdd checkup lint demos/prompt_repair/subscription_billing_after_python.prompt

<vocabulary>
- active subscription: a subscription record with status IN ("active", "trialing")
  and current_period_end > now() in UTC
- billing window: the 24-hour window beginning at 00:00 UTC on the renewal date
- valid payment method: a Stripe PaymentMethod with status "succeeded"
  and card.exp_month/card.exp_year not in the past
- graceful payment failure: returns HTTP 200 with JSON
  {"status": "billing_failed", "next_retry_at": "<ISO-8601 timestamp>"}
  and emits a BILLING_FAILED event to the audit log
- reasonable retry: up to 3 attempts at exponential intervals (1 h, 24 h, 72 h)
  over a 4-day window from the first failure
- successful billing: a Stripe charge whose status transitions to "succeeded"
  and whose associated invoice.status == "paid"
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 - Subscription renewal
The system MUST write a billing_attempt record to the audit log
for all active subscriptions due within the billing window.

R2 - Payment processing
The system MUST charge the valid payment method on file
and return HTTP 200 with a billing receipt JSON body on success.

R3 - Failure handling
The system MUST return HTTP 200 with {"status": "billing_failed",
"next_retry_at": "<ISO-8601>"} and schedule reasonable retry attempts
when a charge fails.

R4 - Customer notification
The system MUST emit a BILLING_SUCCEEDED event to the notification queue
within 5 minutes of successful billing.

R5 - Idempotency
The system MUST NOT double-charge any subscription within the same billing cycle.
</contract_rules>

<requirements>
- Process monthly and annual subscriptions.
- Support USD, EUR, and GBP currencies.
- Write structured audit logs for every billing attempt.
- Expose idempotency_key on all charge requests.
</requirements>
